c Pulmonary Disease with Right Heart Strain", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.05436532064809184, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["The subacute 48-hour onset does not completely exclude thromboembolic pulmonary disease (B4), but is atypical for acute embolic events. This marginally reduces B4's likelihood."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Restrictive Cardiac Conditions with Diastolic Impairment", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.00849458135126435, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Chronic symptoms such as ascites or night sweats are typical of constrictive pericarditis, making their absence a negative predictor for this diagnosis."]}, "B6": {"id": "B6", "label": "Reactive Inflammatory Cardiac Conditions", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.010873064129618368, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Missing typical viral pericarditis symptoms (e.g., chest pain alleviated by sitting forward) weakens support for viral-induced tamponade (B1.1) and reactive inflammatory pericardial disease (B6), though does not fully exclude them."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Viral-Induced Acute Pericardial Effusion with Tamponade", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.1802639579384098, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The recent cold increases suspicion of viral-induced pericardial effusion (B1.1), a common cause of acute pericardial disease. However, without chest pain relieved by sitting forward (a hallmark of viral pericarditis), this evidence remains inconclusive."], "evidence_against": ["Classic signs of viral pericarditis, such as chest pain alleviated by sitting forward, are absent in this patient. This weakens but does not exclude viral etiology (B1.1), necessitating further assessment.", "Missing typical viral pericarditis symptoms (e.g., chest pain alleviated by sitting forward) weakens support for viral-induced tamponade (B1.1) and reactive inflammatory pericardial disease (B6), though does not fully exclude them."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1.1", "B1.1.2", "B1.1.3", "B1.1.4"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the pericardial effusion correlate with recent upper respiratory infection (cold)?", "Are there symptoms of pericarditis, such as chest pain, which is relieved by sitting forward?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["PCR for EBV/CMV", "Pericardial fluid analysis for lymphocytic predominance"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Post-Surgical Pericardial Effusion with Tamponade", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.1802639579384098, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The subacute onset (4 weeks post-surgery) and immobilization increase the plausibility of post-surgical pericardial effusion (B1.2). Surgical pericardial complications can manifest later due to delayed fluid accumulation."], "evidence_against": ["The surgical history lacks direct evidence of pericardial injury or retrograde stasis, which are critical for post-surgical effusion diagnosis (B1.2). This weakens the argument for this sub-branch despite temporal correlation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.2.1", "B1.2.2", "B1.2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the effusion occur within 6 weeks of Achilles tendon surgery?", "Is there evidence of retrograde venous stasis or pericardial injury in surgical history?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Doppler ultrasound for postoperative thrombosis", "CT chest with contrast to evaluate surgical complication"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "management_pathway"}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Neoplastic Pericardial Effusion with Tamponade", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.060331825037707384, "posterior": 0.0643799849780035, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The absence of systemic malignancy signs (weight loss, night sweats) contradicts neoplastic pericardial effusion (B1.3), though ECG findings (low voltage in Figure A) are not explicitly described in the text to confirm or refute this.", "A known malignancy would strongly implicate neoplastic effusion (B1.3), but its absence here supports less ominous subacute causes like viral or post-operative etiologies. This weakens neoplastic pericardial disease as a dominant differentiator."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does the patient have a history of known malignancy or paraneoplastic syndromes?", "Are there signs of systemic illness (weight loss, night sweats) alongside effusion?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["CT/PET for malignancy screening", "Pericardial fluid cytology or tumor markers"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.1.1": {"id": "B1.1.1", "label": "Epstein-Barr Virus (EBV) Induced Pericardial Tamponade", "parent": "B1.1", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.04506598948460245, "posterior": 0.04506598948460245, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Does EBV serology in the context of pericarditis align with recent upper respiratory infection?", "Was the recent cold a known EBV reactivation in this patient?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["EBV DNA PCR in serum/pericardial fluid", "EBV antibody panel (VCA, EA, EBNA)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.1.2": {"id": "B1.1.2", "label": "Cytomegalovirus (CMV) Induced Pericardial Tamponade", "parent": "B1.1", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.04506598948460245, "posterior": 0.04506598948460245, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is the patient immunocompromised (e.g., diabetes, obesity-related metabolic dysfunction) which would heighten CMV suspicion?", "Does the pericardial fluid analysis show high neutrophil counts typical of CMV?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["CMV pp65 antigenemia testing", "CMV DNA PCR in pericardial fluid"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.75, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "management_pathway"}, "B1.1.3": {"id": "B1.1.3", "label": "Coxsackievirus Induced Pericardial Tamponade", "parent": "B1.1", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.04506598948460245, "posterior": 0.04506598948460245, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Are there concurrent signs of myocarditis (e.g., chest pain, arrhythmias) which is common with Coxsackie etiology?", "Did chest X-ray show pericardial calcifications arguing against viral etiology?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Coxsackie B viral culture or PCR", "Pericardial fluid lactate dehydrogenase (LDH) levels"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.4, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.4, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "urgence"}, "B1.1.4": {"id": "B1.1.4", "label": "Parvovirus B19 Induced Pericardial Tamponade", "parent": "B1.1", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.04506598948460245, "posterior": 0.04506598948460245, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there a history of prolonged fever (weeks) typical of parvovirus pericarditis?", "Are there associated symptoms of arthritis or rash suggesting parvovirus?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Parvovirus B19 PCR", "Pericardial fluid viral load testing"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.35, "interrupt_relevance": 0.65, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B1.2.1": {"id": "B1.2.1", "label": "Postoperative Dressler Syndrome (Autoimmune Pericarditis)", "parent": "B1.2", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.06008798597946993, "posterior": 0.06008798597946993, "danger": 0.75, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there a history of recent pericardial or myocardial injury (e.g., cardiac surgery, trauma) that could trigger autoimmune pathophysiology?", "Are there elevated inflammatory markers (ESR, CRP) or evidence of antinuclear antibodies?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["C-reactive protein (CRP) and erythrocyte sedimentation rate (ESR)", "Autoimmune panel (ANA, ANCA, etc.)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B1.2.2": {"id": "B1.2.2", "label": "Postoperative Septic Pericarditis from Distant Surgical Infection", "parent": "B1.2", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.06008798597946993, "posterior": 0.06008798597946993, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is there evidence of sepsis from the surgical site (e.g., wound infection, leukocytosis)?", "Was surgical drainage or culture performed during Achilles repair showing infection?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Blood cultures", "Pericardial fluid Gram stain and culture"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.55, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "test_pathway"}, "B1.2.3": {"id": "B1.2.3", "label": "Postoperative Hemorrhagic Effusion from Anticoagulation Complication", "parent": "B1.2", "level": 3, "status": "live", "prior": 0.06008798597946993, "posterior": 0.06008798597946993, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "reopen_triggers": [], "askable_discriminators": ["Is the patient on anticoagulants (e.g., LMWH) post-surgery that might contribute to bleeding into the pericardium?", "Do coagulation studies show abnormalities (INR, PT/PTT) in this context?"], "requestable_discriminators": ["Coagulation profile (PT/INR, APTT)", "Pericardial fluid cell count and biochemistry (elevated RBC: hemorrhagic effusion)"], "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.3, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.65, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "management_pathway"}}, "frontier": ["B1.3", "B1.1.1", "B1.1.2", "B1.1.3", "B1.1.4", "B1.2.1"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 4, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Is there any evidence in the surgical history (Achilles repair) or clinical course directly indicating pericardial injury (e.g., retrograde venous stasis) that would support a postoperative cause for effusion?", "result_summary": "The surgical history lacks direct evidence of pericardial injury or retrograde stasis, which are critical for post-surgical effusion diagnosis (B1.2). This weakens the argument for this sub-branch despite temporal correlation.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.2": "weak_against", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.3": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral", "B6": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 2, "bundle_id": 2, "bundle_position": 5, "bundle_size": 6, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented systemic malignancy (no cancer history mentioned) argue against neoplastic pericardial effusion as the cause of tamponade?", "result_summary": "A known malignancy would strongly implicate neoplastic effusion (B1.3), but its absence here supports less ominous subacute causes like viral or post-operative etiologies. This weakens neoplastic pericardial disease as a dominant differentiator.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.3": "weak_against", "B1.1": "neutral", "B1.2": "neutral", "B2": "neutral", "B3": "neutral", "B4": "neutral", "B5": "neutral", "B6": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 0, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Could the patient’s surgical history and immobility explain a hypercoagulable state contributing to thromboembolic pulmonary disease (B4) despite echocardiographic findings favoring pericardial pathology?", "result_summary": "Immobility from the recent Achilles repair creates a small risk of hypercoagulability that could plausibly contribute to thromboembolic pulmonary disease (B4), but the echocardiographic findings more clearly support pericardial pathology. This provides minimal support for B4.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B4": "weak_for"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 1, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the recent viral cold (E3) and normal ventricular contractility (E10) support reactive-inflammatory pericardial disease (B6) as the intermediate mechanism for impaired diastolic filling?", "result_summary": "The viral cold and preserved ventricular contractility slightly support reactive inflammatory pericardial disease (B6) as a mechanism for impaired diastolic filling, but the absence of specific fever/migratory symptoms reduces this support. The findings remain neutral for B6.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B6": "neutral"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 2, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the 48-hour time course of worsening dyspnea argue against thromboembolic pulmonary disease (B4), which typically presents as an acute event, compared to cardiac tamponade (B1 sub-branches) that can allow a subacute onset?", "result_summary": "The subacute 48-hour onset does not completely exclude thromboembolic pulmonary disease (B4), but is atypical for acute embolic events. This marginally reduces B4's likelihood.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B4": "weak_against"}}, {"timestep": 3, "bundle_id": 3, "bundle_position": 3, "bundle_size": 4, "action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "external_action": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of febrile symptoms or migratory arthralgias in a patient with a viral cold argue against reactive inflammatory pericardial disease (B1.1/B6) as the cause of impaired diastolic filling?", "result_summary": "Missing typical viral pericarditis symptoms (e.g., chest pain alleviated by sitting forward) weakens support for viral-induced tamponade (B1.1) and reactive inflammatory pericardial disease (B6), though does not fully exclude them.", "per_action_branch_effects": {"B1.1": "weak_against", "B6": "weak_against"}}], "differential_history": [{"B1": 0.6728971962616823, "B2": 0.14018691588785046, "B3": 0.07009345794392523, "B4": 0.07476635514018691, "B5": 0.02336448598130841, "B6": 0.018691588785046728, "B1.1": 0.24790949335956716, "B1.2": 0.24790949335956716, "B1.3": 0.17707820954254797}, {"B1": 0.39819004524886875, "B2": 0.04776269482151834, "B3": 0.02388134741075917, "B4": 0.05094687447628623, "B5": 0.007960449136919723, "B6": 0.012736718619071557, "B1.1": 0.16892911010558068, "B1.2": 0.16892911010558068, "B1.3": 0.060331825037707384}, {"B1": 0.0643799849780035, "B2": 0.0509674881075861, "B3": 0.02548374405379305, "B4": 0.05436532064809184, "B5": 0.00849458135126435, "B6": 0.010873064129618368, "B1.1": 0.1802639579384098, "B1.2": 0.1802639579384098, "B1.3": 0.0643799849780035, "B1.1.1": 0.04506598948460245, "B1.1.2": 0.04506598948460245, "B1.1.3": 0.04506598948460245, "B1.1.4": 0.04506598948460245, "B1.2.1": 0.06008798597946993, "B1.2.2": 0.06008798597946993, "B1.2.3": 0.06008798597946993}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": true, "reason": "Cardiac tamponade is a time-critical syndrome requiring immediate intervention. Signs of Beck variant (pulsus paradoxus >10mmHg) suggest hemodynamic compromise. Impaired diastolic filling on echocardiogram confirms pericardial pathology.", "required_actions": ["Perform emergent pericardiocentesis", "Start IV crystalloids to increase preload"]}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termi