onary Disease with Right Heart Strain", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.040667808219178085, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Acute dyspnea over 48 hours is inconsistent with parvovirus B19’s typical chronic/indolent course, disfavoring its role here."]}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Restrictive Cardiac Conditions with Diastolic Impairment", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.006354345034246577, "danger": 0.55, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Chronic symptoms such as ascites or night sweats are typical of constrictive pericarditis, making their absence a negative predictor for this diagnosis."]}, "B6": {"id": "B6", "label": "Reactive Inflammatory Cardiac Conditions", "level": 1, "status": "closed_for_now", "posterior": 0.008133561643835618, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Missing typical viral pericarditis symptoms (e.g., chest pain alleviated by sitting forward) weakens support for viral-induced tamponade (B1.1) and reactive inflammatory pericardial disease (B6), though does not fully exclude them."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Viral-Induced Acute Pericardial Effusion with Tamponade", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.1802639579384098, "posterior": 0.12810359589041098, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The recent cold increases suspicion of viral-induced pericardial effusion (B1.1), a common cause of acute pericardial disease. However, without chest pain relieved by sitting forward (a hallmark of viral pericarditis), this evidence remains inconclusive."], "evidence_against": ["Classic signs of viral pericarditis, such as chest pain alleviated by sitting forward, are absent in this patient. This weakens but does not exclude viral etiology (B1.1), necessitating further assessment.", "Missing typical viral pericar